<title>UK: NWE oil products pulled lower by falling crude.</title>
<headline>NWE oil products pulled lower by falling crude.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE oil products all felt the affects of weaker crude on Friday.</p>
<p>Gasoline was weaker. Eurograde barges fell to trade at $201 and $201.75 fob ARA.</p>
<p>High and low sulphur fuel oil fell by a dollar or two. High sulphur barges traded at $90 fob ARA.</p>
<p>Gas oil fell sharply knocked lower by tumbling IPE futures although premiums held steady.</p>
<p>Naphtha lost ground to reflect crude's weakness and good supplies.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
